Generic single-database configuration.

LexChiapas policy (see also the comment block at the top of env.py):

- Before the "baseline schema real" revision, this project had NO Alembic
  and NO migration scripts. All schema changes were manual
  `ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS` / `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`
  run by hand against the real DB, with no record in git. The baseline
  revision is a snapshot of that real schema as of the day Alembic was
  adopted -- it intentionally contains no upgrade() operations (the tables
  already exist) and should only ever be applied to an already-populated DB
  via `alembic stamp head`, never `alembic upgrade head` from empty.

- From now on, for any schema change:
  1. Edit the SQLAlchemy model in app/models/*.py.
  2. Run `alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short description"`.
  3. Open the generated file in alembic/versions/ and READ it by hand.
     Autogenerate does not always get pgvector's `vector` type, JSONB
     server_default, or index/constraint naming right -- fix the script
     before applying it, don't apply blindly.
  4. Run `alembic upgrade head` against the real DB.
  5. Commit the migration file together with the model change in the same
     commit.

- Never hand-edit the schema with a raw ALTER TABLE again outside of this
  flow -- that is exactly the pattern Alembic was adopted to replace.
